#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:5
#: 09a2e9c29c7740958c7f9a8bcfab9f01 0f1da9c8c9f54701860a79c4e23eccbb
#: 233e656aaf8d485e85068b98b6a9558c ef52db22a8a54c85b9dd700e7bbaeedb
#: f80dfe30d0aa4478b5164a1665dadb09
msgid "ESC Grounding and Wiring Considerations"
msgstr "ESC 接地与布线注意事项"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:7
#: 2d3eeba5866445ea839bc91403d5c807 3d9d45f9a49c4a7caf1802308ab0cd65
#: 5b66c55be9d44d0b888cd6425f5058dd 71d80bc7dfb34a8ab240b642fe3aedf4
#: 9fa8f0e9438d4f8d9a5195418a86a86b
msgid ""
"On larger, heavier vehicles, very high motor currents can be present leading"
" to several types of signaling issues which may impact reliable motor "
"operation. On smaller vehicles the use of the ESC's BEC (when provided by "
"the ESC) if an autopilot has on-board supply for servos requires special "
"handling."
msgstr ""
"在较大、较重的飞行器上，可能存在非常大的电机电流，导致多种信号问题，影响电机的可靠运行。在较小的飞行器上，如果飞控板载舵机电源使用电调内置的 "
"BEC，则需要特殊处理。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:9
#: 71f0241264f94208959618980c8120c0 b0d2101392ad4fcdbba479d5804356e9
#: be915aaccca741ceb0c1d939a9594eca c8701095215e4c8b87d7e40eacfe71e2
#: dd546d9471b54ec78656e943f3d982be
msgid ""
"ESC grounding issues are made up 3 forms of ESC signalling/coupling "
"problems, resistive, capacitive and inductive. All three should be "
"considered when building an aircraft."
msgstr "ESC 接地问题由三种 ESC 信号/耦合问题构成：阻性、容性和感性。构建飞行器时应综合考虑这三种情况。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:12
#: 5667a3be817b41e4a14a945c9d9cf5f1 65bc8c84cac14e24a1ec7c621b3484b8
#: be03eb63e8c4478f8e7d090df96ab3af c91f575978b94857a5ec865a85e16c88
#: e806553465c64bd89513d4bd5d7315c3
msgid "Inductive"
msgstr "感性"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:14
#: 2e7e233187894c5e8fe989c7a2678ec9 5af916fa6c6343bfb5fe80fd2ee58337
#: 78087428f6e349a3b93fe73aac27fc58 8c4db8358c9d417c9632ebb4c8abc700
#: a5d73551189b4afb8d7816cb0d746efe
msgid ""
"This is the tendency for sudden changes in current to cause large voltage "
"spikes in your system. Inductance in your power system is primarily caused "
"by the size of the loop formed by the positive and negative leads between "
"the ESC and battery. So the longer the cables to the ESC the higher the "
"inductance. However the most important consideration in reducing the "
"inductance is to ensure the positive and negative power wires are kept very "
"close together. This can be done by twisting the two gently together "
"approximately 1 twist every 10 to 20 cm. A 10cm long lead with a large gap "
"between wires will have a much higher inductance than a 1m long lead with "
"minimum spacing between the positive and negative lines."
msgstr ""
"这是电流突变导致系统中出现大电压尖峰的趋势。供电系统中的感抗主要由电调与电池之间正负极线缆所形成的回路面积决定。因此，到电调的线缆越长，感抗越大。然而，降低感抗最重要的措施是确保正负极电源线紧密并排。可以通过每"
" 10 至 20cm 轻轻扭转一次来实现。10cm 长但两线间距大的线缆，其感抗远高于 1m 长但正负线间距最小的线缆。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:16
#: 279c4aaedee24cc1acd07ee0c864167e 649d0da10f524ac6b32638a67519d1e7
#: 804d5c43e12a46a79972046aebb21114 ae7c5136b9734d06867e399e0c4d93e3
#: f442fc37314f4158bbf159aad580b423
msgid ""
"High inductance is like water hammer in the house pipes. Each time the ESC "
"turns off the voltage across the input of the ESC spikes. In extreme cases "
"this can cause damage to the input capacitor or the FETS. This noise can "
"directly cause signal detection problems or commutation detection problems. "
"These voltage spikes can also cause signal detection problems indirectly by "
"capacitive coupling to your PWM signal line. (These spikes are absorbed by "
"the large capacitors on the input of your ESC so your broken capacitor wire "
"will make this type of noise more serious)"
msgstr ""
"高感抗就像房屋水管中的水锤现象。每次电调关断时，电调输入端的电压都会产生尖峰。在极端情况下，这可能损坏输入电容或 "
"MOSFET。这种噪声可能直接导致信号检测问题或换相检测问题。这些电压尖峰还可能通过容性耦合到 PWM "
"信号线而间接造成信号检测问题。（这些尖峰由电调输入端的大电容吸收，因此断裂的电容引线会使此类噪声更为严重）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:20
#: 20fcd5c8c5bf4a8a9f069e430db04066 77803a7539b14cf2a0e90464f449be1e
#: a94e2475d8bc4ad89fdb5e1d85cebfe4 ae433acea14c40408a68ac795eba6207
#: b3b51df504944456b4d7d5383fa07f5c
msgid "Capacitive"
msgstr "容性"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:22
#: 0292d0774a7d4230925d09ee48649121 21dcae13f7f549938c95d3de64f451ff
#: 2223317f98fa4f44b9a7a5ac17dbd082 7526d6a58100442ab67e411dbf718371
#: 83bd2e96ba1342f09903bd3427e0bb88
msgid ""
"Capacitive coupling problems are a result of voltage spikes in large power "
"wires or other devices like radio transmitters being coupled to the PWM "
"wires. ESC’s designed with high impedance terminations and don’t have "
"effective filters on the ESC input can be particularly susceptible to this. "
"BLHeli based systems tend to have less filtering due to the higher data "
"rates required. Bi-directional systems make it even more difficult to "
"effectively filter this noise."
msgstr ""
"容性耦合问题是由大功率线缆或其他设备（如无线电发射机）中的电压尖峰耦合到 PWM "
"线缆所导致的。采用高阻抗终端且电调输入端没有有效滤波器的电调对此尤为敏感。基于 BLHeli "
"的系统由于需要更高的数据速率，滤波通常较少。双向系统使有效滤波此类噪声更加困难。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:24
#: 30e686fed8904b00bd1b41992a519d68 5e9cb834d6bb4e94a81f66931f64f28d
#: 638aa6a5a6c8425d99da744c19cce087 86094211756748cb8ee4d934b09717c9
#: b8dd445bb2944a8d9e4fed007f8bc129
msgid ""
"Capacitive coupling is minimised by using twisted PWM signal wires as an "
"noise source tends to couple equally to both the ground and signal line. It "
"is also good practice to avoid routing PWM lines next to things like radio "
"transmitters or lidars."
msgstr ""
"通过使用双绞 PWM 信号线可以最大程度减少容性耦合，因为噪声源倾向于对地线和信号线产生相等的耦合。同时，避免将 PWM "
"线路与无线电发射机或激光雷达等设备并行布线也是良好实践。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:26
#: 077c70007c224501822ef7ea4dd6a66c 282aa09a52c440c9974326924b7601e2
#: 925383caf43c482eb79e82b46cbdabe8 d19627cc5f564771b8b2d5052c61b6d1
#: dea66dc99c2843f985788bd22dcf5f43
msgid ""
"A common source of this coupled lines is the close proximity of power wires "
"connected to ESC’s. This is a difficult problem to avoid as these wires "
"generally must travel in the same space as the power. In this instance the "
"twisted pair, signal and ground, is the only practical option. Other "
"mitigations focus on reducing the magnitude of this noise source (reduce "
"inductance in the power wires and adding additional capacitance at the ESC)"
msgstr ""
"这种耦合线路的常见来源是连接电调的电源线距离较近。由于这些线路通常必须与电源线在同一空间内走线，因此很难避免。在这种情况下，信号和地线的双绞线是唯一实用的选择。其他缓解措施集中在减小噪声源的幅度（减少电源线中的感抗，并在电调处增加额外电容）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:29
#: 103cafaf6b7349579b4cc0a3db896840 6fe4cc61ac7e4b1e86b31ce7d3d51576
#: 7f3a47405a16441d97095a334af1ebfb a7d8f4848b7040a694957b29143b7664
#: b123f50a303e4c92b2f133f5f9f66ba4
msgid "Resistive"
msgstr "阻性"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:30
#: 0781b499f7b84cd2b932a61cd0dc9681 3998341072a24eadb95dd63ea9be3d01
#: 75531351305c4e078bdf733e997bc056 83358149d4fe4a6e9f365f6fc95a20a0
#: d288988de1394ce3add038ba48f10f67
msgid ""
"This is one of the less well understood coupling mechanisms but is common in"
" many aircraft. The problem stems from the simple fact that the ground or "
"black wires are not 0.0 V. If the negative bullet connector of the battery "
"was at zero volts all other points on the ground line would be at a higher "
"voltage depending on how much current was flowing back towards the battery. "
"It is also important to understand that current will flow back to the "
"battery through all the available ground paths, not just the shortest path."
msgstr ""
"这是较少被理解的耦合机制之一，但在许多飞行器中很常见。问题源于一个简单的事实：地线或黑线并不是 "
"0.0V。如果电池的负极接线端为零伏特，地线上其他所有点的电压都会更高，具体取决于流回电池的电流大小。同样重要的是要理解，电流会通过所有可用的接地路径流回电池，而不仅仅是最短路径。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:32
#: 1c865b47936c44578068080df511cb5e 21f0124696454080a27e0a28d6f81ff9
#: 2f57d89083c84d27aacfaef85178f2de 8f8b61b3968d4f88958f4a9bd4e65e0f
#: e2e39d0d80c74184af9a8fa75b8c8749
msgid ""
"Most Multirotor aircraft have 4 to 8 ESC’s capable of drawing very high peek"
" currents. This current must flow back to the battery and is divided between"
" the main power ground and the signal ground based on their impedance. 22 "
"AWG wire will have an impedance of something of the order of 48 to 67 Ohm "
"per km while 14 AWG wire will be 8 to 12 ohm. This means for the same length"
" of power and signal wire, for every 7 amps of current draw there will be 6 "
"amps in the 14 AWG and 1 amp in the 22 AWG wire. However all these signal "
"wires go back to the autopilot then through 2 to 4 28ish AWG BEC ground "
"wires. 28 AWG wires have an impedance of 200 to 280 Ohms per km."
msgstr ""
"大多数多旋翼飞行器有 4 到 8 个电调，能够汲取非常高的峰值电流。这些电流必须流回电池，并根据阻抗分配在主电源地和信号地之间。22 AWG "
"线缆阻抗约为每千米 48 至 67 欧姆，而 14 AWG 线缆约为每千米 8 至 12 欧姆。这意味着在相同长度的电源线和信号线中，每 7 "
"安培的电流消耗，14 AWG 线缆中有 6 安培，22 AWG 线缆中有 1 安培。然而，所有这些信号线都返回到飞控，再通过 2 到 4 根约 28 "
"AWG 的 BEC 地线。28 AWG 线缆的阻抗为每千米 200 至 280 欧姆。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:34
#: 12c2a97a35c145608a0931759e24d1a2 1d273136606445c688af9b4a7f0e2589
#: 64b556ee5ce24b4ab91fbdf360f03445 7d3036486ace4b08b1bf26112702aa81
#: 87a90a42974c487d81f4a1fa6c0417f2
msgid ""
"The impact of this ground return current in the autopilot BEC wires is an "
"increase in the ground voltage of the autopilot compared to the battery. "
"This often causes current and voltage measurements to read low."
msgstr "这种接地回路电流流过飞控 BEC 线缆的影响是飞控的接地电压相对于电池升高。这通常会导致电流和电压测量值偏低。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:36
#: 4bafc592721144b58332062d2e228d54 58ecf386cc5845d387ba8278c9c6b031
#: a8a8cabc600f443aab2cab14f876b25e b105c3b9b91d40508b2772989ddee036
#: d4fd37137b1a4591a07d5613656a46b2
msgid ""
"The impact of significant current in the ESC signal ground wire is an "
"increase in the ground reference of the ESC compared to the AutoPilot. This "
"makes the peek voltage of the signal line appear lower. Especially when "
"using 3.3 V signalling this can reduce the signal to a point where it is "
"interpreted as a low state, changing the throttle level or interrupting "
"communication in digital systems (CAN is differential so not impacted as it "
"is not ground referenced)."
msgstr ""
"ESC 信号地线中存在较大电流的影响是电调的接地参考电压相对于飞控升高。这使得信号线的峰值电压看起来更低。尤其是在使用 3.3V "
"信号时，这可能将信号降低到被解释为低电平的程度，从而改变油门值或中断数字系统中的通信（CAN 为差分信号，不以地为参考，因此不受影响）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:38
#: 246ffbb8e59f48cc92bbb24e92208cf9 835a52785c1848c1a7f58d9dba8a2926
#: a0dd7dd3e40940fb8fe1b6e602f71985 a96802e4f6a442748f6fd09a148d7eb4
#: ccd5e97380b14da6a426ce400531a28b
msgid "So what does all that mean from a practical standpoint…"
msgstr "那么从实际角度来看，这意味着什么……"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:40
#: 0bf07d46b7784b2ebd899b2a573fa956 47dec2f7ea6349318aac72f672636bf1
#: a5550b61cb4d4b0a91f35e639f77e721 ac02c1cb1cb0436c9776c999e8297ca3
#: afabf88b08a248fb98ddec5026cf481e
msgid ""
"Keep the negative and positive power wires to any component next to each "
"other (touching) over as much of the rout as possible."
msgstr "尽可能使任何组件的负极和正极电源线在整个走线过程中保持相邻（紧贴）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:41
#: 6b9ed17fce7041468c7f3924f2bf3c6b 774ffe752de34a6996b211332347e2e5
#: 978144d6312e40feb3ddcb04ee60d000 ba945398497b4883abdccefc88f6a558
#: ce63d98f0ab147feb461696e5509aabc
msgid "Avoid loops and large gaps between positive and negative power wires."
msgstr "避免正负电源线之间出现环路和较大间隙。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:42
#: 2ad2bf0dd4e64afc9364ceefe9294c22 9242030bcb154c44b52971c7f6281b69
#: 9c9f9f4f381e4d909c199d8a31b1ba62 b35e55ad004245d1848d25cfc6222423
#: d87d8043caff4aa29ba661a53fce048d
msgid ""
"On very long runs to ESC’s additional capacitance may be required at the "
"ESC."
msgstr "对于到 ESC 的走线非常长的情况，可能需要在 ESC 处增加额外的电容。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:43
#: 5542f46dcdae47f1b14dc92a7ba40ac4 59c0211591ff44769adfa5626d41452d
#: 77ded65df6114a71bbc29e364df295ea 9634686769a34d479a59fc484888c450
#: a2fb95fe54724b0a8d5022f77199091e
msgid ""
"Use twisted PWM wires to minimise capacitively coupling to the high "
"impedance signal wires."
msgstr "使用绞合 PWM 线，以尽量减少对高阻抗信号线的容性耦合。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:44
#: 28348975331e4c0b88b18bcebbb622dc 3467642e64ab4cbf92aaba7f90ac33d1
#: 97ec99ef7ab64af98f33dd8253e3bd7f b506a22b9c4e454ab2f5a11d60eeedf6
#: e6c666c659ad48b587339c4be5df9c96
msgid "If possible, use 5V signalling when long runs are present."
msgstr "如果走线较长，尽可能使用 5V 信号电平。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:45
#: 2a3b165d9bbd49a0be8a9803db9e2b0b 4e2634ccaf2e46908f451301e6c4db79
#: 515da54cc66f442ba04c97ba63654a35 6b96713efdb84e6684041af0412f0479
#: a369d6f6ae5c41ee982a6214fe159ebf
msgid ""
"Avoid routing next to noisy components like other ESC’s, ESC wiring, and "
"radios."
msgstr "避免走线靠近其他 ESC、ESC 接线和无线电等噪声较大的组件。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:46
#: 31470028b7ec4697984120a802fab567 6fd6f78301494162af938ef7de27cba2
#: ac90e48e9da04f558122c9f34d311652 d3a419ad6c4744ef996bdd8bdf0834d6
#: ebdae4dca022415bb275296919581896
msgid ""
"Where possible add additional ground connections between the autopilot and "
"system ground."
msgstr "在可能的情况下，在飞控与系统地之间增加额外的地线连接。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:47
#: 1143c7db28e140d685993986d62c81f8 3e3e88a2fa06477782f243c8031a798c
#: c42b039c5f594731a0eef31318440bff d6606d47fdc24aff8f48c913b09b72d8
#: e96eecc0f1fa486d962a81433797d3a5
msgid ""
"Ensure all connections, solder joints, bullets, plugs etc are clean and make"
" good contact."
msgstr "确保所有连接点、焊点、子弹头接头、插头等清洁并接触良好。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:50
#: 4ea79a1acc9449db9c9c3e4954463b83 5bfabac50a0543df84a2b2ed086b37cc
#: 70d1a4d576464683afadc07c91910b44 927409b74c6747bda49badd304d3ee23
#: ea5f47a30fd94cb0a03d067b5611ea86
msgid "ESC BEC Considerations"
msgstr "ESC BEC 注意事项"

#: ../../source/docs/common-esc-grounding.rst:52
#: 1e94e90cfd9a4ed5bc48ed06c4063646 78b02711052f41999b41ede2f749c5f4
#: 7bf34e2df90f4be5a9479eb7ab626886 9c310834043b4666b56b4d1cd185d740
#: f7ced748ffb64fb09ef0172afb28b61f
msgid ""
"Smaller vehicels often employ autopilots that have integrated power supplies"
" for attached servos. ESCs used in these smaller vehicles often also provide"
" their own BEC for powering servos in receiver only base systems. It is "
"recommended to not attach the ESC's BEC leads to the autopilot's servo "
"supply rail if it provides its own supply."
msgstr ""
"较小的飞行器通常使用集成了舵机供电电源的飞控。这类小型飞行器中使用的 ESC 通常也为仅使用接收机的基础系统提供自带的 BEC "
"来为舵机供电。如果飞控本身已提供舵机供电轨，建议不要将 ESC 的 BEC 引线接入飞控的舵机供电轨。"
